The chat betwwen me and Xujin

Madhurima:

My analysis aligns with yours. One small difference in how we traced it: you found segment_start = -1 (no HEADER candidates at all) and context coming from "4 Generator" SECTION_HDR at 3171 directly. I arrived at the same conclusion from the other direction by looking at what context_candidates resolved to and why context_type ended up as Generator.
Root cause is two things stacked:
The TOC entry "4 Generator" was being picked up as a live section header because the SECTION_HDR loops had no toc_cutoff guard. This set context_type to Generator across the entire document body. When the preprocessor hit 3.8.7 Rotor, the guardrail blocked it.
Rotor was not in the SUBSEC_TURBINE pattern, so it had no independent detection path when context was unavailable or wrong.
Fix I am applying to preprocessor_v2:
Add toc_cutoff guard to both SECTION_HDR loops so TOC entries are excluded from body context.
Add Rotor to the SUBSEC_TURBINE pattern so it is detected independently of context.
Add flip-back logic in the inference step so Rotor headings skip the nearest-sibling lookup and inherit from the Gas Turbine parent instead.
After the fix, 3.8.6 Generator ends at 60359 and 3.8.7 Rotor gets its own Gas Turbine / 298464 region. The chunk split will restore automatically when P1 and P2 are rerun.

Since this touches the SECTION_HDR context logic and SUBSEC_TURBINE pattern, it is a fairly broad change that could affect other documents. I think after the fix, we should run the full regression in the ds_test tables first and leave the dev tables intact. Once the regression passes we can promote to dev tables, so that we have a baseline.

